# mm.mcu

A portable microcontroller hardware interface, in partitions by facility. It
declares what a platform may supply and translates the results into typed C++; it
implements nothing. Every entry point calls an extern "C" function that a board,
an adapter, or a test defines, because a name attached to a module cannot be
defined by a translation unit outside that module and a platform's implementation
is always outside.

Partitions are listed before the primary interface because source order is
declared, and the primary re-exports them.
